// cppcheck suppression list for gbglow
//
// Per-symbol unusedFunction suppressions live inline, as
// `// cppcheck-suppress unusedFunction` directly above the symbol, so they
// travel with the code instead of breaking whenever a file shifts by a line.
// build.sh passes --inline-suppr, which is what makes those effective.
//
// Only path-wide suppressions that have no single line to attach to remain here.

// --- Third-party libraries in external/ or vendor/ - not our code, not our findings ---
*:external/*
*:src/vendor/*
